      "result": "\n\nDone. The complete C source is written to `submission/main.c`.\n\nSummary of what's in it:\n\n- **Device**: `DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(spi0))` with a `device_is_ready()` check that prints an error and returns `-ENODEV` if not ready.\n- **Buffers**: `tx_data[8]` = `0x01…0x08`, `rx_data[8]` zero-initialized.\n- **Config**: `struct spi_config` with `.frequency = 1000000` and `.operation = SPI_OP_MODE_MASTER | SPI_WORD_SET(8)`.\n- **Descriptors**: `struct spi_buf` (tx/rx, each `.len = 8`) wrapped in `struct spi_buf_set` with `.count = 1`.\n- **Transfer**: `spi_transceive(spi_dev, &spi_cfg, &tx_bufs, &rx_bufs)`; a negative return is printed and propagated.\n- **Verification**: byte-by-byte `tx_data[i] != rx_data[i]` comparison — prints `\"SPI loopback successful\"` on full match, `\"SPI loopback mismatch\"` on any byte difference (returning 0 / `-EIO` respectively).\n\nHeaders included: `zephyr/kernel.h`, `zephyr/device.h`, `zephyr/drivers/spi.h`, `string.h` (plus `errno.h` for the `ENODEV`/`EIO` return codes).",
